If you think with an ambiguous language, you vaguely know what you are
thinking about. If you are thinking in Lojban you know precisly what you are
thinking about. This is one of the advantages of Lojban over RARbau.


The other advantage, is that currenntly a Lojban programming language is in
development. Once it is fully implemented, expressing yourself in Lojban, or
lojSAMban if the Lojban community isn't willing to accept whatever
modifications will be necessary to fully disambiguate the language --
doesn't seem like we'll need to do anything funky atm, already made a parser
and working on the .jbo to .pl conversion right now.

